From fe62b922d7a79e0abae208568fbee8ceac1cec22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 07:31:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban sync: hold run rows while behind, busy rounds
 are skipped, chunked reconcile pull

Review 5887313221 of PR #1934 (t_01a1d36ddcea59fe):

- A round that stops behind the feed head now holds task_runs rows on its post-pull send too
  (push(hold_runs=...), _send(after_pull=, hold_runs=)). Sent whole, a pending run start overwrote
  an end the Board held in an unread page (reclaimed -> running) and its ack fenced the end off.
- SyncRoundBusy from sync_board (routine now that dispatch_tick holds the board lock) is a skipped
  round: DEBUG only, the board is not marked failed, outbox_age keeps its last verdict, and the loop
  retries after BUSY_RETRY_S (0.5 s). The zero wait comes from this round's results, not from the
  process-wide backlog flag a skipped round leaves stale.
- reconcile pulls the replica to the head in PULL_PAGE_BUDGET chunks (backlog.replica_at_head) and
  releases the board between them, so sync rounds (and their pushes) run during a long catch-up; it
  waits out busy rounds for up to RECONCILE_BUSY_WAIT_S in all.
- dispatch_tick keeps going only on BoardBudgetExhausted; a raw read TimeoutError stays a recorded
  pull error.
- The outbox-age alarm leaves out run rows while the board is behind (they are held on purpose).
- Dead `or PushResult()` fallback removed.

Tests: 6 new in test_kanban_sync_push_starvation.py, each red on 20f21b13ea.
